esp32s31: stop RX halting after one period

Capture had never worked: recording failed with EIO after exactly one period,
which is what made "bring up I2S capture" look like unfinished bring-up rather
than a one-bit bug.

hw_params builds a single control word from the TX field definitions and writes
it to whichever direction is being configured. Every field it sets sits at the
same bit in both registers - msb_shift 13, tdm_en 19, bck_div_num 26:21,
checked against the SoC header - except the one at bit 4:

    TX_CONF bit 4      tx_stop_en    stop when the FIFO empties
    RX_CONF bits 5:4   rx_stop_mode  0 = run until rx_start clears
                                     1 = also stop when in_suc_eof is 1

So writing the transmit value into RX_CONF asked the receiver to stop as soon
as the first DMA descriptor completed. One period, then nothing.

There is a second, unrelated trap worth recording: the RX path of the AHB GDMA
keeps one descriptor per period and rejects period_len > 4095, while the I2S
driver advertises period_bytes_max = 4096. A capture that picks the advertised
maximum therefore fails in dmaengine_prep_dma_cyclic(), which the PCM layer
reports as -ENOMEM from soc_component_trigger - not an obvious pointer to an
off-by-one. Periods of 4095 bytes or fewer work; the advertised limit should
be lowered for capture, which is left for the mic bring-up.

With this, recording runs continuously and returns full-length files. The mic
input path itself is still not producing live audio - two captures come back
byte-identical, every sample a constant -5504 - so the ADC routing remains to
be brought up.

--- a/sound/soc/espressif/esp32s31-i2s.c
+++ b/sound/soc/espressif/esp32s31-i2s.c
@@ -45,6 +45,8 @@
 #define ESP32S31_I2S_TX_START		BIT(2)
 #define ESP32S31_I2S_TX_SLAVE_MOD	BIT(3)
 #define ESP32S31_I2S_TX_STOP_EN		BIT(4)
+/* RX_CONF instead has a two-bit stop *mode* here; 0 = run until stopped. */
+#define ESP32S31_I2S_RX_STOP_MODE	GENMASK(5, 4)
 #define ESP32S31_I2S_TX_CHAN_EQUAL	BIT(5)
 #define ESP32S31_I2S_TX_MONO		BIT(6)
 #define ESP32S31_I2S_TX_BIG_ENDIAN	BIT(7)
@@ -267,10 +269,23 @@
 	i2s->sysclk_hz = mclk;
 
 	/* Philips I2S: data delayed one BCLK from the word select edge. */
-	conf = ESP32S31_I2S_TX_MSB_SHIFT | ESP32S31_I2S_TX_STOP_EN |
-	       ESP32S31_I2S_TX_TDM_EN |
+	conf = ESP32S31_I2S_TX_MSB_SHIFT | ESP32S31_I2S_TX_TDM_EN |
 	       FIELD_PREP(ESP32S31_I2S_TX_BCK_DIV_NUM, bck_div - 1);
 	/*
+	 * TX_STOP_EN is bit 4 of TX_CONF and belongs to transmit alone. RX_CONF
+	 * uses bits [5:4] for rx_stop_mode, where 1 means "stop when rx_start
+	 * is 0 **or in_suc_eof is 1**" - so writing the transmit value into
+	 * RX_CONF halted capture the instant the first DMA descriptor
+	 * completed. That is why recording produced exactly one period and then
+	 * failed with EIO, and why capture had never worked.
+	 *
+	 * Every other field this builds sits at the same position in both
+	 * registers (msb_shift 13, tdm_en 19, bck_div_num 26:21, checked
+	 * against the SoC header), so only this one has to be conditional.
+	 */
+	if (playback)
+		conf |= ESP32S31_I2S_TX_STOP_EN;
+	/*
 	 * Slots are exactly as wide as the samples, so the slot width, the
 	 * half-frame width and the WS pulse width are all the sample width.
 	 */
